    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78557" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπετάννῠμαι</span></b> , pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πέπτᾰμαι</span> (in pres. sense),
			v. infr. :—
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be hung
			before</i>, pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πεπετας μένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					33.5.2
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>to be stretched, extend along</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαιῇ παραπέπταται ἰσθμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					98
				</span></i>
			, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπέπταται Ὄρνις</span> the Bird (i.
			e. Cygnus) <i>hovers before</i> it <i>with outspread wings</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				312
			</span></i>.</div>
